  "At easier levels, move slowly until you learn the movement.": "På lättare nivåer, rör dig långsamt tills du lär dig rörelsen.",
  "At least 120 min of scheduled Zone 2 and about 51 min of hard cardio a week; controlled vigorous blocks on Tuesday, Thursday and Saturday.": "Minst 120 min schemalagd zon 2 och cirka 51 min hård cardio i veckan; kontrollerade kraftfulla block tisdag, torsdag och lördag.",
  "At New to training and Returning, keep the pace brisk and below all-out effort. At Active, work hard. At Well trained, use all-out effort.": "At New to training and Returning, håll farten högt och under all ansträngning. At Active, jobba hårt. At Well trained, använd all ansträngning.",
  "At Returning and above, hold a dumbbell in each hand, or loop a band around your waist with its anchor in front of you. The band should pull you forward, like a sled.": "At Returning and above, håll en hantel i varje hand eller ögla ett band runt midjan med ankaret framför dig. Bandet ska dra dig framåt, som en släde.",
  "At Returning, push back up with your hands. At higher levels, pull yourself back with your hamstrings.": "At Returning, tryck uppåt med händerna. At higher levels, dra dig tillbaka med dina hamstrings.",
  "At the end of your last interval, note your peak heart rate. Walk gently for 60 seconds and note your heart rate again. Enter the drop (peak minus 60s reading).": "I slutet av ditt sista intervall, notera din topppuls. Gå försiktigt i 60 sekunder och notera din puls igen. Gå in i droppen (topp minus 60s avläsning).",
